<title>USA: GOLF-LEADERS UPON COMPLETION OF FIRST ROUND OF INTERNATIONAL.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEADERS UPON COMPLETION OF FIRST ROUND OF INTERNATIONAL.</headline>
<dateline>CASTLE ROCK, Colorado 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scores</p>
<p>after completion of the weather-hit first round at the $1.7</p>
<p>million Sprint International played on the 7,559-yard, par-72</p>
<p>Castle Pines course (U.S. unless noted):</p>
<p>(Tournament is played under the modified Stableford format</p>
<p>that awards five points for eagle, two for birdie, zero for</p>
<p>par, and subtracts one point for bogey, three points for</p>
<p>double bogey or worse.)</p>
<p>15 - Larry Mize, Jay Haas</p>
<p>14 - Phil Mickelson</p>
<p>13 - Tom Lehman</p>
<p>12 - Dave Stockton junior</p>
<p>11 - Scott McCarron, Andrew Magee</p>
<p>10 - Olin Browne, Brad Faxon, Dudley Hart, Hideki Kase</p>
<p>(Japan), Skip Kendall</p>
<p>9 - Stewart Cink, Stuart Appleby (Australia), Scott Simpson,</p>
<p>Kenny Perry, Greg Norman (Australia)</p>
<p>8 - Tommy Armour, Neal Lancaster, Jimmy Green, Grant Waite</p>
<p>(New Zealand), Kirk Triplett, Gary Hallberg, Brian Henninger,</p>
<p>Brent Geiberger, Craig Kanada</p>
<p>Other international golfers</p>
<p>6 - Nick Price (Zimbabwe)</p>
<p>5 - Ernie Els (South Africa), Peter Lonard (Australia),</p>
<p>Retief Goosen (South Africa)</p>
<p>3 - Yutaka Hagawa (Japan)</p>
<p>0 - Nick Faldo (Britain)</p>
<p>-2 - Brad Hughes (Australia), Mike Weir (Canada)</p>
<p>-3 - Rafael Alarcon (Mexico) -12 - Phil Tataurangi (New</p>
<p>Zealand)</p>
</text>
